cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "Rarefaction Review Benchmark: Reproducibility Package"

message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite the associated manuscript
  and this repository.

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Tokoro
    given-names: Shunji
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8042-9869"
    affiliation: "Gifu University of Medical Science"

repository-code: "https://github.com/shunjit/rarefaction-review-benchmark"

url: "https://github.com/shunjit/rarefaction-review-benchmark"

abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for the manuscript "Rarefaction validity is task-dependent: justified for microbiome diversity, harmful for differential abundance, reportable via a decision framework". This repository contains the
  scripts, metadata, and documentation required to reproduce the benchmark
  analyses evaluating rarefaction practices for microbiome diversity analysis
  using three public 16S rRNA amplicon datasets, together with the code,
  frozen run configurations, and summary outputs of the depth-confounding
  differential abundance benchmark introduced in revision.

keywords:
  - microbiome
  - rarefaction
  - QIIME2
  - 16S rRNA
  - diversity analysis
  - differential abundance
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark

license: MIT

